# Local development settings. Copy to `.env` — this folder is where the app
# looks. Real environment variables ALWAYS win over this file, so a deployment
# can never be reconfigured by a .env that was committed by accident.
#
# An empty file is fine: the app runs on SQLite and a local folder by default.

# ── Cloudflare R2 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Paste these exactly as Cloudflare gives them. Filling in all four switches
# file storage to R2 on its own — STORAGE_BACKEND is not needed.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=          # from your dashboard URL; builds the endpoint
# R2_BUCKET_NAME=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=       # R2 API token, permission "Object Read & Write"
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#
# R2_PUBLIC_URL is NOT used, and does not need to be set. Files are served
# through the API, which checks who owns a run first; a public bucket URL
# would hand out other people's carbon data to anyone with the link.

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Omit for local SQLite. A provider's own URL works as injected.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/clear

# ── Task queue ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Omit and the three long jobs run in background threads, as they always have.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# ── CORS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed when the frontend is on a different domain than this API.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://clear.vercel.app
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN_REGEX=https://clear-.*\.vercel\.app
